    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d203-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0377" n="337" xml:id="pg337"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Earl Russell</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 1, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> It is with deep concern that I hasten
                    to communicate to your lordship the painful intelligence I have just officially
                    received of the death of Abraham Lincoln, late President of the United States,
                    who was assassinated in Washington city on the evening or the 14th ultimo, and
                    expired the next morning from the effects of the wound.</p>
                <p>In communicating this melancholy event I feel persuaded that your lordship and
                    the British nation will not fail to participate in the general grief into which
                    this sudden calamity has plunged the people of the United States.</p>
                <p>I pray your lordship to accept the assurances of the highest consideration with
                    which</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, my lord, your lordship’s most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FEANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl Russell,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
